#: content/guides.ts
msgid "'Open source' on a clipping tool can mean anything from a fully local pipeline to a thin client that still calls one vendor's API. The question that matters is whether you can run every step on your own hardware, with the models you choose. Reelsaw was built to answer yes to both; OpenShorts, the other open-source clipper with traction, can pick moments locally, but Gemini is still required for layout picking and silent videos."
msgstr "'Open source' on a clipping tool can mean anything from a fully local pipeline to a thin client that still calls one vendor's API. The question that matters is whether you can run every step on your own hardware, with the models you choose. Reelsaw was built to answer yes to both; OpenShorts, the other open-source clipper with traction, can pick moments locally, but Gemini is still required for layout picking and silent videos."

